/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  PROPOSAL (review 2026-11-12) -- NOT a tutorial, NOT validated, NOT in the
  corpus.  Once-through electrodialysis of a wine drawn from a stratified vat.

  THE PROCESS, as declared for this proposal: wine is drawn from the BOTTOM of a
  vat, deionised in ONE pass through the stack and returned at the TOP through
  a diffuser; the treated wine is lighter and stays on top, so the vat is a
  displacement vessel, not a stirred tank.  The operator sets a target for the
  treated wine's conductivity (20 % below the wine's); the current that gives
  it is HELD and the voltage rises as the membranes foul, up to 2 V per cell
  pair; at that limit the current falls and the membranes are cleaned.  The
  vat is finished when the conductivity of the wine ENTERING the machine
  FALLS (the treated layer has reached the draw-off).  Vat 10 000 L.

  HOW THIS FILE REPRESENTS IT, and every workaround named:
  * VAT is the UNTREATED wine only, a variable-volume vessel drained at the
    circulation flow (3000 L/h, the industrial stack record's design flow).
    In a perfectly stratified vat the treated wine never meets the untreated
    again, so it leaves the model as the product stream `treated`.  The end
    of the vat is then the vessel running dry at V/Q = 10 m3 / 3 m3/h =
    3.33 h; the engine REFUSES the dry vessel (measured: "the vessel RAN DRY
    at t = 12010 s"), so endTime stops short of it.  The FALL of the inlet
    conductivity at the end is interface mixing, which no vessel here models.
  * `vatBottomInlet` is a trace flow (1e-9 kmol/h): a vessel must declare an
    inlet and a zero-flow one is refused ("molarComposition sums to zero").
  * A variable-volume vessel needs a liquid density, and the ion records
    carry no Vliq: the run REFUSES without one.  The scratch probe gave every
    ion water's Vliq (no physical claim); this proposal does NOT ship that
    placeholder -- curating it, or a dilute-carrier density rule for vessels,
    is a named gap.
  * ED is the steady `electrodialysisStack` wrapped `quasiSteady`, on
    `targetConductivityRemoval 0.20` -- the unit SOLVES the current, which
    stands in for the operator's control loop (a PID cannot actuate a
    quasi-steady unit: "does not expose MV").  No fouling is modelled, so the
    voltage does not rise from fouling at all.
  * BRINE is a 200 L constant-volume tank primed with KHT 20 mol/m3 (author-
    set; citric acid is not in the tree).  Its drain-to-50-L / refill cycle is
    NOT represented (no conditional event in this binary; a `recipe` block is
    silently ignored), and a closed constant-volume loop lets the circulating
    molar flow drift with the ions it gains.
  * `stack industrialStack50m2;` is a TOKEN: substitute the identifier of the
    catalogue's industrial `kind edStack` record of 50 m2 cell-pair area.
    constant/ is ed09_wine_multiionic's, unsealed (the wine of ed09: thirteen
    ions, ethanol absent, author-set composition).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
units
(
    {
        name        VAT;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          vatBottomInlet;
        outputs     ( toStack );
        operation
        {
            energy      isothermal;
            UA          0.0;
            T_jacket    298.15 K;
            volumeMode  variable;
            geometry    { shape verticalCylinder; diameter 2.0 m; height 3.6 m; }
            outflow     { mode flow; F 0.04631425838; }
        }
    }
    {
        name        BRINE;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          brineOut;
        outputs     ( brineIn );
        operation   { energy isothermal; UA 0.0; T_jacket 298.15 K; }
    }
    {
        name        ED;
        type        quasiSteady;
        inputs      ( toStack  brineIn );
        outputs     ( treated  brineOut );
        unit
        {
            type        electrodialysisStack;
            operation
            {
                stack                      industrialStack50m2;
                membrane                   CMX_AMX;
                targetConductivityRemoval  0.20;
                xi                         0.9;
                E_electrodes               2.0;
            }
        }
    }
);
